      },
      {
        "str": "Abstract",
        "transform": [8.9664, 0, 0, 8.9664, 285.854, 482.31899999999996],
        "width": 40.578339840000005,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "",
        "transform": [8.831904, 0, 0, 8.9664, 110.726, 468.333],
        "width": 0,
        "height": 0
      },
      {
        "str": "Transformers are slow and memory-hungry on long sequences, since the time and memory complexity",
        "transform": [8.831904, 0, 0, 8.9664, 110.726, 468.333],
        "width": 404.71228570559987,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "of self-attention are quadratic in sequence length.",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.907, 457.374],
        "width": 208.76770391039997,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": " ",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 305.6747039104, 457.374],
        "width": 6.769632000000021,
        "height": 0
      },
      {
        "str": "Approximate attention methods have attempted",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 312.57972855040003, 457.374],
        "width": 202.51568424960018,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "to address this problem by trading off model quality to reduce the compute complexity, but often do",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.907, 446.415],
        "width": 418.18475450879976,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "not achieve wall-clock speedup. We argue that a missing principle is making attention algorithms",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.907, 435.456],
        "width": 401.84408229119964,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": " ",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 498.7510822912, 435.456],
        "width": 3.0959977537254617,
        "height": 0
      },
      {
        "str": "IO-",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 501.909, 435.456],
        "width": 14.172220108800001,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "aware",
        "transform": [8.9305344, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.201, 424.497],
        "width": 23.067570355199994,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "—accounting for reads and writes between levels of GPU memory. We propose",
        "transform": [8.9305344, 0, 0, 8.9664, 119.948, 424.497],
        "width": 317.20990272768,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": " ",
        "transform": [8.9305344, 0, 0, 8.9664, 437.15790272768, 424.497],
        "width": 3.07640288385542,
        "height": 0
      },
      {
        "str": "FlashAttention",
        "transform": [8.9305344, 0, 0, 8.9664, 440.222, 424.497],
        "width": 73.60189231104002,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": ",",
        "transform": [8.9305344, 0, 0, 8.9664, 513.825, 424.497],
        "width": 2.54877451776,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "an IO-aware exact attention algorithm that uses tiling to reduce the number of memory reads/writes",
        "transform": [9.145728, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.907, 413.538],
        "width": 418.18841279999987,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "between GPU high bandwidth memory (HBM) and GPU on-chip SRAM. We analyze the IO complexity",
        "transform": [8.876736, 0, 0, 8.9664, 96.907, 402.579],
        "width": 418.5318886847996,
        "height": 8.9664
      },
      {
        "str": "of",
